# Model endpoint behind the Lab 01b relay (demystifying how AI thinks).
#
# Copy this file to gravwell-llm.env (same directory; git-ignored) and fill in a real endpoint. The
# endpoint is Ollama-shaped (/api/generate, /api/embed, /api/tags): a hosted model with a bearer
# token, or your own Ollama with LLM_UPSTREAM_TOKEN left empty. Rotate the token after every class.
#
# It never reaches a seat. start-llm-relay.sh copies these values to /opt/workshop/gravwell-llm.env
# (root, 0600) and a root systemd service (llm_relay.py) listens on 127.0.0.1:9010, adding the bearer
# token on the way out. Seats get only GRAVWELL_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9010 in ~/.workshop_env; the
# lab scripts send no credential. build-student-repo.sh reads this file and refuses to publish if the
# token string appears anywhere in the staged student repo. /opt/workshop/.env may override.
#
# Models: the lab scripts default to MODEL=logbot and EMBED_MODEL=qwen3-embedding; set MODEL and
# EMBED_MODEL in the seats' environment (makeuser.sh) if your endpoint serves different names.
LLM_UPSTREAM_URL="https://model.example.com"
LLM_UPSTREAM_TOKEN="REPLACE-ME"
